[{:name "bridge-strict-and-closed-convergence-in-measure-thresholds"
  :level :strategy
  :status :draft
  :maturity :one-shot-heuristic
  :body
  {:problem-class
   "A problem states convergence in measure with strict bad sets `{x | ε < |fₙ x - g x|}` and strict measure bounds, while the library API uses closed bad sets `{x | ε ≤ dist (fₙ x) (g x)}` whose measures tend to zero."
   :proof-shape
   ["Keep a problem-faithful definition rather than silently replacing `>` by `≤`."
    "For the problem-to-library direction, unfold `tendstoInMeasure_iff_dist` and `ENNReal.tendsto_atTop_zero`. Given library distance threshold `ε` and target measure bound `b`, handle `b = ⊤` separately; otherwise choose `δ = min ε b.toReal / 2`."
    "Use `{x | ε ≤ dist (fₙ x) (g x)} ⊆ {x | δ < |fₙ x - g x|}`, measure monotonicity, and `ENNReal.ofReal δ ≤ b`."
    "Shift the problem witness from `N₀ < n` to the library tail convention `N₀ + 1 ≤ n`."
    "For the library-to-problem direction, query the library limit at threshold `ε / 2`, include `{x | ε < |fₙ x - g x|}` in `{x | ε / 2 ≤ |fₙ x - g x|}`, and finish with `ofReal (ε / 2) < ofReal ε`."]
   :preconditions
   ["real-valued functions, so `Real.dist_eq` relates distance and absolute difference"
    "the library convergence predicate exposes closed-threshold bad sets"
    "measure values are in `ENNReal`, including a possible `⊤` target during the limit proof"]
   :boundary
   "The halving/slack argument transfers the convergence predicate; it does not itself construct the almost-everywhere convergent subsequence."
   :key-api
   ["tendstoInMeasure_iff_dist"
    "ENNReal.tendsto_atTop_zero"
    "ENNReal.toReal_pos"
    "ENNReal.ofReal_le_iff_le_toReal"
    "measure_mono"]}
