 {:name "uniformly-continuous-image-boundedness-api-chain"
  :level :lemma-location
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:problem-class
   "Show that a real-valued function uniformly continuous on the open interval `(0,1)` has bounded image, despite the domain not being compact."
   :api-chain
   [{:lemma "`totallyBounded_Ioo 0 1`"
     :role "establish total boundedness of the interval as a set"}
    {:lemma "`isUniformEmbedding_subtype_val`"
     :role "relate total boundedness of the set to total boundedness of the interval subtype"}
    {:lemma "`totallyBounded_image_iff h_emb.isUniformInducing`"
     :role "transfer total boundedness through the subtype inclusion and identify the subtype universe"}
    {:lemma "`TotallyBounded.image`"
     :role "map the totally bounded subtype universe through the uniformly continuous restriction of f"}
    {:lemma "`TotallyBounded.isBounded`"
     :role "turn total boundedness of the image into metric boundedness"}
    {:lemma "`Metric.isBounded_iff_subset_closedBall 0`"
     :role "extract a numerical radius B usable by arithmetic proofs"}]
   :bridge
   "Use `Metric.uniformContinuousOn_iff` to convert the problem-local ε-δ predicate into `UniformContinuousOn`, then use the restriction `I01.restrict f` as the uniformly continuous map on the subtype."
   :result-shape
   "Obtain `∃ B, ∀ x ∈ Set.Ioo 0 1, |f x| ≤ B` after rewriting the restricted image back to `f '' Set.Ioo 0 1`."
   :boundary
   "`TotallyBounded.image` expects a uniformly continuous function on a type; the subtype restriction and uniform-embedding transfer are essential rather than cosmetic coercion fixes."}
